<p>Every one of them is O(n) or close to it — they replace an O(n²) nested loop by touching each element a fixed, small number of times (entering/leaving a window, being pushed/popped from a stack). Recognising which family a problem belongs to is worth more than memorising any single solution; the rest of this deck gives one template per family plus several applications.</p>
