<table>
<thead><tr><th>Rule</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>sort first</td><td>duplicates must sit next to each other for the skip to work</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>if (i &gt; start &amp;&amp; a[i] == a[i-1]) continue</code></td><td>this exact value already tried at this depth: skip to avoid a duplicate combination</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>go(a, i + 1, ...)</code></td><td>each index used once — the reuse trick of slide 11 is gone</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>if (a[i] &gt; remain) break</code></td><td>sorted array: nothing further in the loop can fit either, stop the whole loop, not just this iteration</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
