<p class="meo">🧠 <code>&gt;&gt;</code> = arithmetic shift (keeps sign, for signed division-like behavior); <code>&gt;&gt;&gt;</code> = logical shift (fills with 0, treats the bits as unsigned) — mixing them up on a negative number is a classic bug.</p>
